~ locked
Traveller: An iron gate, cut straight into the rock. Locked, and not the kind you put a shoulder through.
Traveller: [[There's a keyhole. Which means there's a key.|Somebody shut this and took the key with them.|The bars are worn smooth in one place. It has been opened before.]]
=> END

~ hold_key
Traveller: The key is in my bag, not in my hand. Select it on the hotbar, then try again.
=> END

~ unlock
Traveller: The key turns. [wait=0.6]So this is the way the smith meant.
=> END

~ stumps
Traveller: Old stumps, the cuts gone grey. Somebody cut their way through here long ago.
Traveller: [[They were going the same way I am.|Whoever it was, they did not come back this way.|The axe marks are all on one side. They only went in.]]
=> END
